thwip is in public beta.

If your team runs CI on developer machines or coding agents, and you still want a
GitHub-enforced record of what ran on which tree, this is the surface we built
for that job.

{% cta-row %}
{% cta href="/blog/beta-install/" label="Install and sign up" /%}
{% cta href="/dashboard" label="Open the dashboard" variant="ghost" /%}
{% /cta-row %}

## What ships in beta

- A CLI, `@recallnet/thwip`, that runs your required checks, signs a compact
  proof over the exact Git tree, and attaches it as a commit trailer.
- A GitHub App that verifies those proofs against current repository
  permission, enrolled signing keys, and project policy.
- Organization and project controls on [thwip.recall.net](https://thwip.recall.net),
  mirrored from GitHub membership. No separate invite system.
- Two security profiles you can set per path: **fast** (signed local proof) and
  **remote** (GitHub runs the checks and signs provenance).

## What a proof is (and is not)

A thwip proof is a signed claim: who ran the approved checks, on which Git tree,
under which policy version, with a key enrolled to a GitHub account that still
holds repository permission.

thwip never sees your source and never watches your test process. False claims
are caught when digests disagree with other machines, later commits, or a remote
profile run—not by surveillance.

{% callout type="tip" title="Precision" %}
The remote profile is SLSA Build L3 for the checks GitHub actually ran. Fast is
an attributed assertion plus hermeticity and reproducibility controls. Pick
remote where a cloud re-run is worth the minutes.
{% /callout %}

## Who beta is for

- Teams where agents or developers already run lint, typecheck, and tests
  locally, and replaying everything in Actions is pure latency.
- Orgs that want the merge queue gated on *evidence*, not on “CI green on a
  different SHA.”
- People who will read the [FAQ](/faq) before treating a proof as stronger than
  it is.

## Pricing while we learn

Free and Pro both verify the same way. Free is capped for projects and signers;
Pro raises those caps. Details stay on the dashboard and in
[llms.txt](/llms.txt).

